    "name": "consecutive-max-the-run-spans-the-thirty-first-into-the-first",
    "why": "A run spanning the month boundary is ONE run, and its length is only knowable from the carry-in tail: 30 and 31 July are in the already-published month and 1 and 2 August are in the horizon, so the cap of three is broken on the 2nd. Horizon-local evaluation sees a run of two and reports nothing at all -- which is the defect this whole tail exists to prevent, and it is invisible on any mid-month corpus. The violation is located inside the horizon; the two July dates are read as context and never re-reported.",
